# Vercel builds from the repo root, configured that way in vercel.json.
# Everything the frontend build does not need is excluded here so the upload
# stays small.
#
# backend/ is not listed: the API is its own Vercel project with Root Directory
# set to backend, and Vercel applies this repo-root file to that project too.
# Ignoring backend/ here strips every file before the Python build runs.
#
# The build no longer reads contract/ — that was the mocks, which are gone. The
# root-level build is now only a deployment setting, not a dependency. Leave it
# as it is until after the event; retargeting the build is not a thing to try
# on a day the site has to stay up.

data/
docs/
PROPOSAL+REGULATIONS/
.impeccable/
.claude/
*.md
!frontend/**/*.md
